{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question","id":589629,"title":"Blood and Smoke Combat Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-13T16:48:48-07:00","id":589629,"title":"Blood and Smoke Combat Question","content":"I tried searching around, and did not find anything referencing this, so if I missed it, please point me to where it is. In B&amp;S, defense goes up, but attack dice do not. Its possible for a starting character to have a 13 defense (not counting merits)! Even with this being reduced with each successive attacker, each round, it would take 5, STR 5 Brawl 5 assailants to get a single attack at greater than a chance die. This just seems broken to me. Or, to a more realistic scenario, a STR 2 Brawl 2 attacker has a chance die versus a Wits/Dex 2 Athletics 2 defender. Two equally matched combatants, 10% chance to hit.<br /> <br /> My conclusion: I must have missed something. What am I doing wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6924-tunglashr","name":"tunglashr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:00:59-07:00","id":589652,"title":"","content":"Spend a willpower +3 dice, go all out +2 dice, generally in 2nd edition, fisticuffs miss a lot (thanks to the high defense) unless people are going all out. also remember specialties apply to attacks, but not defense. Also some fighting styles put damage out each round (kung fu, heavy weapons) and just a single hit, will add all weapon damage in auto successes... Also fireams ignore defense... <br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry on mobile made this difficult to organize...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:04:47-07:00","id":589654,"title":"","content":"That's a white room, one in a million character design that's so fixated on having high defense that you might as well give it to them?<br /> <br /> Like, you're talking someone with Wits 5 and Dexterity 5, Athletics 5 and Celerity 3.<br /> <br /> That person has ridiculously low attributes in all other things, and if I were being myself with my players, I would ask them how this is a real person.<br /> <br /> If you're entertaining this character concept, than they have invested <i>so much </i>into dodging <i>everything </i>then I have to ask you, why bother taking that away?<br /> <br /> Besides, it's not as if they'll be in a great position to hit anything, either.<br /> <br /> You could also build a Strength 5, Brawl 5 Vigor 3 character who has a dice pool of +13 to hit, but it's the same scenario. 1. That's ridiculous. 2. if they <i>really </i>want to do that <i>so bad</i> why deprive them of it?<br /> <br /> and to deal with both of these things, you have the fact that they reduced their other stats to nil just to get there. It's certainly not gonna be any easier to resist getting mind controlled, or shot (FYI only that +3 defense from Celerity will apply if the opponent has a gun) or any other numerous things that could happen to a character.<br /> <br /> So yeah, if you're not building an actual human being and instead going for a punch machine/dodge machine, this could be a problem, but it's one quickly negated by numerous other solutions.<br /> <br /> As for the situation where the two are evenly matched: Presumably, they'll use Willpower and get the leg up on their opponent. Maybe they'll also use an All-Out Attack. If they have a weapon, they might be able to hit you hard enough to Tilt you with even a basic attack (especially if you're a mortal) but they might also arm wrack you, forcing you to drop your weapon and disadvantage you.<br /> <br /> Or they miss, and their All-out Attack has sacrificed their defense, and you take the opportunity to tilt them yourself.<br /> <br /> Or if you'vre the attacker with Brawl, maybe you try to intitiate a Grapple so that suddenly, that Defense score is a whole lot less relevant.<br /> <br /> Don't forget you've probably got merits on top of all that to further tip things in one direction or another.<br /> <br /> AND if you're a Vampire, you could also spend a Vitae for Physical Intensity.<br /> <br /> So let's take this situation of the STR 2 Brawl 2 guy versus the Wits/Dex Ath 2 defender. They're both BP 1. STR 2 Brawl 2 guy spends a Willpower, makes an All-out Attack and spends a Vitae. Suddenly he's got a whopping +7 extra dice to hurt you with. Nice! If he hits you, he'll probably grapple you, and then he could spend the Willpower and Vitae again for +5 on the contested strength roll, giving him a major advantage to... I dunno, bite you with his fangs and do Lethal. Scary!<br /> <br /> Or if he misses, he's defenseless, and if you're also STR 2 with Brawl 2, you could then make that same move he just did, except he doesn't benefit from defense. So you've got a dicepool of +11 in that situation. Maybe you take a penalty to inflict a Tilt, so that even when his Defense is back, it's still hobbled. Congratulations, you are now advantaged.<br /> <br /> This completely fails to take into account additional factors like environment, allies and other things that can add up, but trust me, combat is fine in practice. It can be pretty fun once you realize there's more to it than just making regular attacks until they die. Fight smart. This ALSO doesn't take into account situations where Beaten Down and Surrender might be in effect. In the above situation, if you get off that Willpower + All-out Attack, you might score enough damage to inflict Beaten Down on someone, which might lead to them just surrendering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-13-2015, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:05:01-07:00","id":589655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tunglashr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question#post589629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its possible for a starting character to have a 13 defense (not counting merits)!</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like the kind of senseless min-maxing I would condone at a table I was running. Assuming we're talking about a standard starting character anways.<br /> <br /> And you didn't really miss anything. See also every factor that Hackthulhu pointed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:07:20-07:00","id":589657,"title":"","content":"It's working as intended. If you dump all of your character creation resources into being hard to hit, you should be very hard to hit. You're also not accounting for Vigor, Willpower, Physical Intensity, and bonus dice from Frenzy. If this Dex 5, Wits 5, Athletics 5, Celerity 3 character goes up against a Strength 5, Brawl 5, Vigor 3, BP 3 character (also possible at character creation), the attacker can frenzy, spend Willpower, and spend 2 Vitae for physical intensity and 1 for increased damage from Vigor, they'd have a total dice pool of 10 <i>after</i> subtracting Defense, and deal +3 damage on a hit. If they use Weaponry instead of Brawl, they'd have a very easy time getting the 5 damage required to stake the opponent. It's also worth noting that both of these characters are one-trick ponies, and this white room analysis doesn't account for a great deal of the realities of game play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:08:39-07:00","id":589658,"title":"","content":"You've got that exactly right. WoD 2e did a great deal of beefing up of both attack and defense options, and its totally possible to build a character with colossal defense or exceptional armor. Of course, the reverse is also true and one can create a character with exceptional damage and accuracy. Or all of the above.<br /> <br /> Combat in WoD 2e is not the standard exchange of dice until one person runs out of hit points. Cunning, circumstance and (let's face it) pure luck play a big part. The system doesn't shy away from letting characters be <b>good</b> at things. You can build a starting character who will buzzsaw through people like butter and the system will support you. And that might be a broken if WoD was a tactical combat game like Dungeons and Dragons. But it is not. There are ample ways for a character with high defense to get screwed over, mind effects, surprise attacks, superior armor, hell one lucky it with a sledge hammer would be enough to drop (or nearly drop) a mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 07-13-2015, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:28:27-07:00","id":589689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589657#post589657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's working as intended. If you dump all of your character creation resources into being hard to hit, you should be very hard to hit. You're also not accounting for Vigor, Willpower, Physical Intensity, and bonus dice from Frenzy. If this Dex 5, Wits 5, Athletics 5, Celerity 3 character goes up against a Strength 5, Brawl 5, Vigor 3, BP 3 character (also possible at character creation), the attacker can frenzy, spend Willpower, and spend 2 Vitae for physical intensity and 1 for increased damage from Vigor, they'd have a total dice pool of 10 <i>after</i> subtracting Defense, and deal +3 damage on a hit. If they use Weaponry instead of Brawl, they'd have a very easy time getting the 5 damage required to stake the opponent. It's also worth noting that both of these characters are one-trick ponies, and this white room analysis doesn't account for a great deal of the realities of game play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So two evenly matched opponents should have a 10% chance to hit each other unless they spend willpower? That is as intended? <br /> <br /> The ridiculous example is exactly that, and noted. But two normal, reasonable characters have chance dice against each other. There are exactly three words that describe this: bad game design.<br /> <br /> If this were a non-combat situation involving a non-combat skill, and you had a character who had 2 dots in that skill, and was attempting an average difficultly action, you should expect to have around an 80% chance to succeed, no willpower necessary. But somehow, everyone in the world has forgotten how to do anything related to hand to hand combat. Either you are forced to spend a limited resource or forgo your defense to get a reasonable hit chance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The system doesn't shy away from letting characters be <b>good</b> at things. </div> </div> </div>Sure it does, hand to hand combat as evidenced above.<br /> <br /> If the normal situation in a game is completely broken because of all the possible crazy things the system tries to account for, then the veracity of those crazy things need to be seriously questioned. Evenly matched characters should not be relegated to a chance die. Arguing otherwise is like screaming at 2+2. No matter how loud you are, its still 4.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6924-tunglashr","name":"tunglashr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:40:02-07:00","id":589693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tunglashr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589689#post589689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So two evenly matched opponents should have a 10% chance to hit each other unless they spend willpower? That is as intended?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, spending Willpower is a thing, so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tunglashr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589689#post589689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ridiculous example is exactly that, and noted. But two normal, reasonable characters have chance dice against each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because there are a lot more ways to raise your attack dice pool than there are to raise your Defense. First of all, attack only requires one Attribute, while Defense requires two. Second of all, as established above, Willpower expenditure is a thing, as is Physical Intensity, bonuses from Frenzy, and Skill Specialties (and the Area of Expertise Merit). And there are a lot of ways to cripple an opponent's Defense, such as multiple attacks, aimed attacks, grappling, and Tilts. It's actually really easy to get around a high Defense character in this system, as long as you don't stubbornly refuse to do anything creative or spend any resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tunglashr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589689#post589689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are exactly three words that describe this: bad game design.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an opinion, not an objective fact. If you don't like it, you are free to play 1st edition, or use house rules. But many people do like the system as it is now. Just let those people enjoy it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:51:45-07:00","id":589697,"title":"","content":"Hyper specialization is a thing. Deal with it. High defense isn't unmanageable, and is in fact so easy to circumvent that dedicating that much to it is a bit of a waste imo. So it becomes hard for your average hand to hand fighter to deal with it, so what? That's what it's there for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:54:38-07:00","id":589699,"title":"","content":"If you want to kill people faster, you can always do things the way they used to be, and remove Athletics from Defense.<br /> <br /> Willpower isn't a rare elusive resource in 2e, and that figures into the action economy. You get it faster, you spend it faster, and it seems to reasonably reflect that, when people are trying to kill you, you're probably trying <i>really hard </i>to kill them first.<br /> <br /> Or whatever your Intent goal is.<br /> <br /> And I can tell you from a solid year or so of actual gaming with Blood &amp; Smoke that it <i>does </i>work, and it works really well, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-13-2015, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:56:09-07:00","id":589701,"title":"","content":"Attacks are less likely to inflict damage in 2e, but more likely to inflict higher amounts of damage when they do inflict damage. The Beaten Down rule is another consideration; any amount of lethal damage is expected to put the hurt on somebody who's fighting for less than extreme odds, and nearly all weapons now do lethal damage (though, of course, not so much against Kindred).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tunglashr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589689#post589689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So two evenly matched opponents should have a 10% chance to hit each other unless they spend willpower? That is as intended?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you weren't spending Willpower in combat, honestly, yeah, that part was kind of unintended. Willpower, especially in 2e, is meant to be spent liberally, recovered and spent again. There's a sidebar emphasizing that in the initial 1e Rules Update; I'm not sure if it made it into the Vampire 2e core. You spend Willpower when you need to depend on something to succeed. If a serious combat situation with some kind of 13 Defense battle ninja isn't a situation where you would strain and push yourself every turn to the greatest extent you can, well, you're either entirely too laid back for your own good, or you're probably that crazy dude who can beat a 13 Defense by 10 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:58:59-07:00","id":589703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tunglashr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589689#post589689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the normal situation in a game is completely broken because of all the possible crazy things the system tries to account for, then the veracity of those crazy things need to be seriously questioned. Evenly matched characters should not be relegated to a chance die. Arguing otherwise is like screaming at 2+2. No matter how loud you are, its still 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;normal situation&quot; you've described is a fantasy, a white room in which two stacks of dice roll off for victory. Evenly matched characters won't exist, not in the sense you are proposing. Even if their dice pools are perfectly even (which is pretty rare), the two fighters are going to have resources at their disposal. Combat options like weapons, willpower, combat styles, not to mention the creativity of the player. You say the system tries to account for too much, but its quite the opposite. WoD expects the storyteller to weigh in with penalties, conditions and set pieces. And it expects the players to actually think about their actions, get creative and give life to the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T18:06:44-07:00","id":589704,"title":"","content":"Solution to the problem:<br /> <br /> Get your friends. Or random hobos, if you are lacking people.<br /> <br /> Play a game. You can play your build.<br /> <br /> Come back once you have some play experience with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T18:10:18-07:00","id":589705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589654#post589654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That person has ridiculously low attributes in all other things, and if I were being myself with my players, I would ask them how this is a real person..</div> </div> </div> </div>International dodgeball champion. Practices with Nascar and stunt drivers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-13-2015, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T18:19:43-07:00","id":589724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589705#post589705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">International dodgeball champion. Practices with Nascar and stunt drivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there, the question is answered!<br /> <br /> Some combination of Ben Stiller in <i>Dodgeball</i> and Vin Diesel in the <i>Fast &amp; Furious</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T18:20:22-07:00","id":589735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589705#post589705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">International dodgeball champion. Practices with Nascar and stunt drivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you can justify pretty much any attribute/skill spread if you try hard enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T18:40:48-07:00","id":589772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589735#post589735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you can justify pretty much any attribute/skill spread if you try hard enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer to think of it as using extreme spreads to justify really different stories. Sarcasm asides, so long as the backstory suggests an interesting story arc and unique consequences, the extremes put forth are just as fine a character concept as any other one. There's no wrong way to do this sort of thing. I mean, solidifying it a little bit-hang on a second.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589724#post589724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there, the question is answered!<br /> <br /> Some combination of Ben Stiller in <i>Dodgeball</i> and Vin Diesel in the <i>Fast &amp; Furious</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there we go. Imagine someone with on-screen Vin Diesel intensity doing Dodgeball. People get crazy passionate about things, and that can lead to a lot of depreciation of other things in life. Sure, the guy's scary and intense to watch on the court, and that makes him amazing in a fight as well, but he's super quiet, and when he talks, it's all awkward as hell. Dude's even more at the top of his game in unlife, but since he has to work at night, this creates problems. What happens when the blessing becomes a curse, when his old way of life is no longer viable? You've taken a beast of a man in his hyperspecialization and taken him out of his context, and he can't go back in. What's more, his ability is passive in a lot of ways. Sure, he can throw knives as well as balls, so he's not bad as an enforcer, but the dude was in for the game, and this sort of thing...well, good question time. Did Dodgeball become passionless for him, so the transition is smooth? Does that bother him? Does that make him wonder what he was really living for? If he was still in it for the fun of the game, then an enforcer's role is not going to gel with him. It was okay when dodgeball was the only thing he needed in life, but now he needs to reach out to someone even if he's going to try and return to his old ways and get away with it, and that mean living beyond his sport. Can he do it? Will he keep himself as he tries?<br /> <br /> So you have a character who's just had everything ripped out from under him and now is wondering where to go with himself, and if he even can go anywhere else. Is he already set to surrender to the Beast, just a slight shove away from sliding down the blood-slick ramp of his humanity? Or can he find something new to live for, or even defy the world and bring his passion into the Society of the Night?<br /> <br /> Much like a white-room scenario is useless without context, base assumptions about attributes-as-character don't mean much until we consider them in the right context. Can White Room Combat happen in a game? Sure. Shouldn't be the norm, because that's boring, but maybe it goes Shonen Jump style at the end and all that matters is what the character brings to the table. Can stories be used to justify having awesome attributes and nothing else? Sure, but it cuts both ways-attributes can suggest a dynamic story if one's willing to tear it apart.<br /> <br /> Broad readings. You can do a lot with them.<br /> <br /> That's why the answer to the OP's question is &quot;Go try this in a game and see if it happens.&quot; Because in here, it's all just icons on a screen.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Can we get a movie of this? Vin Diesel as Dodgeball Ben Stiller trying to control his thirst for blood and live beyond himself while bringing the game of dodgeball into the Society of Night? I'd pay to see that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-13-2015, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T19:01:40-07:00","id":589787,"title":"","content":"10% chance to hit an equally skilled opponent every 3 seconds sounds about right honestly... At least from sparring matches I have been in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T19:07:09-07:00","id":589789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hackthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589787#post589787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10% chance to hit an equally skilled opponent every 3 seconds sounds about right honestly... At least from sparring matches I have been in...</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically solid, damaging hits at that. Glancing blows, partial connects, blocked shots, and hits that are shrugged off are all represented by the misses in this system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T19:55:00-07:00","id":589826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589699#post589699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower isn't a rare elusive resource in 2e</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have problems with 2e combat, but I just haven't found this to be true at all. My group had maybe one or two people (out of three players) gain one or two Willpower between them over a dozen sessions.<br /> <br /> Mask/Dirge require particularly specific circumstances, usually to some extreme degree, for you to see any Willpower. This usually means derailing the campaign specifically for each player to have a chance to regain Willpower.<br /> <br /> Touchstones (I vaguely recall them being an alternate method) require players specifically go out of their way to derail things and meet up with their Touchstone to gain Willpower that way.<br /> <br /> I've basically had to rely on timeskips to refresh people to full, because people have to derail the campaign to get so much as a point back. That only really even works because I have maybe one fight every four or so sessions, so people aren't spending a lot of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T20:12:10-07:00","id":589828,"title":"","content":"I was referring to general 2e, but I can see how vampire can have that problem. For what it's worth, my group allows characters to regain Willpower by acting in line with their Mask or Dirge.<br /> <br /> Ideally Touchstones aren't &quot;derailing things&quot; because they're a component of play, but I'd give characters a Willpower any time they have a scene involving their touchstones, since that qualifies as a meaningful interaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T20:38:26-07:00","id":589838,"title":"","content":"It helps that there's a lot to do other than 'I attack the target.' If you're noticing you aren't hitting, you have Willpower but you also have All-Out Attacks, you can grapple and shake up the dynamic, if the issue is with Weaponry you can try to disarm, you can pull a gun. Werewolves can throw people's Athletics out the window and shift to different forms with different bonuses, making that 10% chance to hit a 10% chance to do +2 lethal and initiate a grapple, vampires can spend Vitae to get a bonus to their physical rolls or, if they are out for blood, frenzy.<br /> <br /> If the characters are just going to stand there having a slap fight they're going to have a slap fight, with all the consequences.<br /> <br /> My character hasn't met his good twin and found himself in a perfectly symmetrical battle, and though I'm sure it would be frustrating, in that situation one must think outside the box.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://33.media.tumblr.com/9834314389b9f57323f59843e3e5d15b/tumblr_mtm50oDvIl1r2x0k1o2_400.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-13-2015, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T20:48:03-07:00","id":589839,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no, one should not plan on an even stevens fight. They don't exist, and if they do, they still shouldn't exist as a majority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T21:22:59-07:00","id":589887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589826#post589826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have problems with 2e combat, but I just haven't found this to be true at all. My group had maybe one or two people (out of three players) gain one or two Willpower between them over a dozen sessions.<br /> <br /> Mask/Dirge require particularly specific circumstances, usually to some extreme degree, for you to see any Willpower. This usually means derailing the campaign specifically for each player to have a chance to regain Willpower.<br /> <br /> Touchstones (I vaguely recall them being an alternate method) require players specifically go out of their way to derail things and meet up with their Touchstone to gain Willpower that way.<br /> <br /> I've basically had to rely on timeskips to refresh people to full, because people have to derail the campaign to get so much as a point back. That only really even works because I have maybe one fight every four or so sessions, so people aren't spending a lot of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often do you pester the storyteller? Are you as a storyteller not including their touchstones for some reason? Or inadvertantly? One of the best things to do as a vampire storyteller is to threaten touch stones... Are the characters not acting in line with their mask/dirge? You shouldn't bend over backwards to give characters willpower back, but if they are playing true to the character it honestly shouldn't be that difficult...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T21:41:46-07:00","id":589892,"title":"","content":"Their Defense means nothing to Majesty, Dominate, Nightmare, Obfuscate, Auspex, Cruac, or Theban Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Their Defense means little to nothing to a gun.<br /> <br /> Their Defense means little to the person with the two-dot Cheap Shot Merit. <br /> <br /> Their Defense means little to a person who invested in Status. <br /> <br /> Their Defense pales in comparison to a relatively average Kindred combatant with moderately high stats, all-out attacks, Willpower, and Vitae.<br /> <br /> Establishing that 13 Defense takes a lot of your starting points. Overcoming a 13 Defense does not take many points at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T12:18:54-07:00","id":590389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589826#post589826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have problems with 2e combat, but I just haven't found this to be true at all. My group had maybe one or two people (out of three players) gain one or two Willpower between them over a dozen sessions.<br /> <br /> Mask/Dirge require particularly specific circumstances, usually to some extreme degree, for you to see any Willpower. This usually means derailing the campaign specifically for each player to have a chance to regain Willpower.<br /> <br /> Touchstones (I vaguely recall them being an alternate method) require players specifically go out of their way to derail things and meet up with their Touchstone to gain Willpower that way.<br /> <br /> I've basically had to rely on timeskips to refresh people to full, because people have to derail the campaign to get so much as a point back. That only really even works because I have maybe one fight every four or so sessions, so people aren't spending a lot of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've talked about this before, and I don't mean to pick at it, but you shouldn't have to do anything extreme to get a single Willpower point from your Mask or Dirge. As the book says, err on the side of giving the point.<br /> <br /> For Mask, you just have to overcome some small hurdle in keeping up your front. Are you a Guru? Get a point by giving advice that sounds good, or by propping up your authority on a subject when it's called into question.<br /> <br /> Dirge isn't meant to actually be harder, but may be difficult if you consider doing a scene for one or two players to be derailing the chronicle. The default mode of play for <i>Vampire</i> involves characters pursuing their own goals (in addition to the coterie's goals) and living their own (so-called) lives. So they get their own spotlight scenes. That said, err on the side of giving points out. If a character is a Monster and kicks the crap out of someone, give the player a point.<br /> <br /> For a game that's more action-procedural, you can make up archetypes to suit team roles, and give out Willpower for fulfilling those. For example, use the archetypes from the <i>Leverage</i> RPG: Grifter, Hacker, Hitter, Mastermind, Thief.<br /> <br /> Touchstones can also be woven into the procedural part of a chronicle. On <i>Forever Knight</i>, we see a lot of Natalie because it's a cop show and she's the one doing the autopsies. On <i>Angel</i>, Angel interacts with Kate because they're solving the same cases, and later with Eve because she's his link to the Senior Partners. (Cordelia, a full member of Angel's team, would also be an easy Touchstone, but she's probably a PC.) <i>Kindred: The Embraced</i> is basically the story of all of the PCs who insisted on taking Frank as a Touchstone. Laura is Carmilla's Touchstone, and that's easy because they live together.<br /> <br /> An easy way to inject more Willpower into a game is to hand it out in addition to Beats. (I often do this <i>instead of</i> Beats for one-shots.) Player hits a character's Aspiration? Give them a point of Willpower on top of their Beat.<br /> <br /> You can also give out extra Willpower the way you might give out extra Beats. Player has a good roleplay moment? Take a point.<br /> <br /> Another option is to give vampires a point of Willpower for sleep, like humans.<br /> <br /> Finally, you can refresh Willpower at the beginning of game sessions, rather than at the usual intervals. Whether this works or not depends on how many scenes your sessions run and how much combat you're doing. Generally, if you run moderate-to-long and/or fighty, giving players Willpower at the start of a session works well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 07-14-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T12:33:29-07:00","id":590398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589826#post589826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mask/Dirge require particularly specific circumstances, usually to some extreme degree, for you to see any Willpower. This usually means derailing the campaign specifically for each player to have a chance to regain Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I think a lot of people miss is that for the example Masques and Dirges, the actions listed are explicitly called out as <i>sample</i> actions that regain Willpower. They're not all you regain Willpower from. For Masques and Dirges you get Willpower for:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire: The Requiem 2nd edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Any time a vampire overcomes a small hurdle in defense of<br /> her Mask, she gains a point of Willpower. When committing<br /> atrocious or existentially risky acts in defense of her Mask, she<br /> regains all her spent Willpower points.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Any time a vampire withdraws from his outside life in<br /> defense of his truer self, he gains a point of Willpower. When<br /> committing terrible, damning acts in defense of his personal<br /> identity, he regains all his spent Willpower points.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>These activities should be some of the main meat of the campaign and a lot of what your stories revolve around. If they're not...well, the game is sort of designed around it.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of folks run into problems with Willpower in Requiem because their campaigns focus around fundementally different things than what the book assumes they do. If that's the case, you're going to want to switch up Willpower gaining methods so that players get rewarded for particpating in the activities you see as being the focus of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589826#post589826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones (I vaguely recall them being an alternate method) require players specifically go out of their way to derail things and meet up with their Touchstone to gain Willpower that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if you're finding Touchstones are derailing things, you might want to consider taking them out and replacing them with something else. If you don't find that interacting with Touchstones is a pretty natural part of what you want to focus your game on, ripping them out is probably smart and replacing them with something else. Like, if instead of focusing on humanity and the interplay because your character's vampire life and the human life they're leaving behind, instead you focus on vampire politics, maybe replace Touchstones with like &quot;Alliegences&quot; or something like that and have characters refocus by getting in touch with their vampire political loyalties. If you run an Underworld-style game where folks are going around doing like missions against the enemies of vampirekind, you can replace Touchstones with &quot;Missions&quot; or something, and have characters do tasks to forward their mission in order to get the same benefits from connecting with Touchstones, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T13:36:49-07:00","id":590453,"title":"","content":"As a rule of thumb for all the 2nd edition WoD:<br /> <br /> Give willpower almost every scene. Give lots of willpower every awesome scene.<br /> <br /> Mask, Dirge, Blood, Bone, Vice, it doesn't matter. In the end, what the game intends to do is to set a tone for the characters behavior, giving the player a quirk to interpret. Every time he does so, he should recover a single willpower point, and to do so should be easy enough to be accomplished almost allways. It isn't something to derail the game, it is something to set the tone of how the character plays out in any scene without stepping out of it.<br /> <br /> The full willpower reward is a little trickier, but sums up to be the Higher Calling of the character: when the character achieves to FOCUS an important scene upon his Calling, he deserves to refresh all willpower.<br /> <br /> Vampire just add a little twist or two. Once by turning both Quirk and Higher Calling into the same thing. Second by turning the quirk a little harder to come by, but just a little, so you can introduce the interaction with Touchstones as a personal moment, even if inside another scene.<br /> <br /> You can twist those rules however you want if they're not working. If you can't find a rule of your liking, just give a willpower point for each character at the end of each scene, and a full recover now and them when they are low on willpower and need to get ready to kick some serious ass, by combat or otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T17:55:34-07:00","id":590652,"title":"","content":"If i may make a suggestion to anyone who thinks Defence is too high? Have the formula be [Lowest of Dex + Wits] + [Athletics/2] + Celerity. In other words, only add half of Athletics (round up) instead of all of it. That has the effect of capping Defence at 8 instead of 10 for mortals and 13 instead of 15 for Vampires. It's not a big difference, really just a small tweak, but one that i think makes the balance of close quarters combat feel a lot better on the whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1450-lys","name":"Lys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1450_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"480"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T19:54:02-07:00","id":590714,"title":"","content":"A lot more replies to my post than I expected. Thank you, everyone.<br /> <br /> Rose's mention of spotlight scenes helped me realize what my real difficulty is in running Vampire. One of the cardinal sins of GMing is, I've always understood, splitting the party. That combined with running exclusively online games (where it's even easier to lose players' attention and never even know it) makes me super reluctant to run &quot;spotlight scenes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given that Vampire is designed around allowing for them (which, it seems, is the source of most/all of my concerns with the system), maybe I just need to buckle down and risk trying it out.<br /> <br /> Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T20:34:07-07:00","id":590776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590714#post590714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose's mention of spotlight scenes helped me realize what my real difficulty is in running Vampire. One of the cardinal sins of GMing is, I've always understood, splitting the party.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love splitting the party. I've always thought that adage was invented for games like D&amp;D where party splitting means greater risk of character death, and in that kind of game I fully agree. But in games like Vampire that are more focused on political maneuvering, or like vanilla World of Darkness that are more about mystery and investigation, I've always found party splitting to be a very useful tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T20:51:44-07:00","id":590788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590776#post590776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love splitting the party. I've always thought that adage was invented for games like D&amp;D where party splitting means greater risk of character death, and in that kind of game I fully agree. But in games like Vampire that are more focused on political maneuvering, or like vanilla World of Darkness that are more about mystery and investigation, I've always found party splitting to be a very useful tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. In my experience, &quot;don't split the party&quot; spells death for a Vampire chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T20:57:45-07:00","id":590792,"title":"","content":"Do you guys run scenes with different characters concurrently, or do one at a time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T21:00:22-07:00","id":590794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590788#post590788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. In my experience, &quot;don't split the party&quot; spells death for a Vampire chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't split the party is among the worst storytelling advice I can imagine, and betrays a deep distrust of the storyteller (who, it is assumed, will seize the opportunity to afflict all forms torments upon the disparate groups).<br /> <br /> Splitting the party gives the storyteller the opportunity to 'cut' from scene to scene as action rises and falls, breeds openings for distrust, conniving and misinformation. More importantly it allows characters of considerable power disparity to shine independent from one another, provides opportunities for challenges that a full party would easily thwart and gives characters a chance for more intimate development. Perhaps most importantly, it's realistic and actually how lives (both real and storied) play out.<br /> <br /> Basically, split the party. Split it often and with impunity until the very concept of a 'party' (a tiresome D&amp;D holdover) is disillusioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T21:27:38-07:00","id":590829,"title":"","content":"Huh. I've only rarely been a player, and I'd never been one when I'd started running my own games, so I'm pretty self-taught. I always understood it to be more for logistic reasons. People get bored. It's easy to lose track of details. It makes things all-around difficult to keep track of. I'm certainly not the sort to try and murder my players' characters.<br /> <br /> Guess I really do have to try it, then, if that's the main concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T21:50:05-07:00","id":590836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590829#post590829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I've only rarely been a player, and I'd never been one when I'd started running my own games, so I'm pretty self-taught. I always understood it to be more for logistic reasons. People get bored. It's easy to lose track of details. It makes things all-around difficult to keep track of. I'm certainly not the sort to try and murder my players' characters.<br /> <br /> Guess I really do have to try it, then, if that's the main concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are, of course, limits. A four way split is likely to be too much, unless your players are really invested in the action (which is entirely possible to achieve). But in general I find players more than willing to spend some time on the sidelines if they know it will mean they get the spotlight in a few minutes. Interestingly I find it cuts down on power gaming as well, if there is no one to show up there is less reason to twink out.<br /> <br /> If you've got the right players you can go for some non-standard structures: I've had player antagonists, split opposing parties, lone wolf characters, characters who spent the majority of the session on the sidelines. In other words, there are no rules, it doesn't matter if two characters are starting, one is an antagonist, a forth has a personal agenda, and the fifth is basically a spectator. If your players are enjoying themselves then the game is good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:12:42-07:00","id":590887,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't jump to conclusions on either side. I do split the party, and know it can be fun. By the way, I do it in D&amp;D, also, so the idea that such is a sin in D&amp;D or in more combat oriented games isn't true. By the way, there's a lot of things you can do in this kind of game where you do need to split the party, and it doesn't have to do with &quot;killing our maiming your PCs&quot;.<br /> <br /> This kind of advice is born precisely from what Maina said. Splitting the party demands its own kind of logistics. As everything else, is pretty much intuitive for some STs, but not so for everyone. Know your players, know your limits and know your timing. Try it a few times prepared to cut scenes in the middle if needed to jump to others, so no one gets bored. Get your hang of this, and them go ahead to do it more oftem.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't go as far as to say there are no such a thing as a party. There certainly are: YOUR party, with ST and players. The characters can be pretty much at each others throats, or even unaware of their existence, but you shouldn't forget the party around the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:28:45-07:00","id":590964,"title":"","content":"IMO a good session of a game should run like a good episode of television. Productive, tense and interesting even if you aren't the focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:51:44-07:00","id":590970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590792#post590792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys run scenes with different characters concurrently, or do one at a time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I know what you mean. But the timing is something that just takes practice. You want to give each group enough time to be satisfying, without leaving the rest waiting for too long. The more separate groups there are, the less time you can spend giving each group the spotlight. But, people are willing to wait longer if the spotlighted action is engaging to listen to. When possible, leaving one group on a cliffhanger when you swing the focus to another group can also increase the drama. It helps me to think about it kind of like an ensemble television show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:58:43-07:00","id":590989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590794#post590794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't split the party is among the worst storytelling advice I can imagine, and betrays a deep distrust of the storyteller (who, it is assumed, will seize the opportunity to afflict all forms torments upon the disparate groups).<br /> <br /> Splitting the party gives the storyteller the opportunity to 'cut' from scene to scene as action rises and falls, breeds openings for distrust, conniving and misinformation. More importantly it allows characters of considerable power disparity to shine independent from one another, provides opportunities for challenges that a full party would easily thwart and gives characters a chance for more intimate development. Perhaps most importantly, it's realistic and actually how lives (both real and storied) play out.<br /> <br /> Basically, split the party. Split it often and with impunity until the very concept of a 'party' (a tiresome D&amp;D holdover) is disillusioned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mind if I repeat this in other mediums, PenDragon? It is really good advice for Storytelling games and those like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T00:34:08-07:00","id":591007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590792#post590792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys run scenes with different characters concurrently, or do one at a time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Both. I've also run flashbacks, montages, scenes that cut between two locations, scenes that occur more than once from different character's perspectives, and scenes that were skipped entirely (the notable example being when a PC; badass vampire duelist, ran head to head with a were-bird-thing. Instead of play the scene I just cut to when other characters arrived to find the vampire drenched in blood, none of which was his own, and a dead bird-thing beside him. This was in the first fifteen minutes of chapter one, Instantly established his badassery in a manner that was pleasing to player and spectators alike).<br /> <br /> Basically, if it works in a book, radio play, comic or television it can probably work in a roleplaying game. Assuming the player(s) is down for it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590989#post590989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind if I repeat this in other mediums, PenDragon? It is really good advice for Storytelling games and those like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quote away my good fellow. <br /> <br /> Though you might drop the D&amp;D bit, as monteparnas said, splitting the party works just as well in D&amp;D. Assuming the DM isn't a vindictive butt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T07:44:47-07:00","id":591296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590714#post590714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot more replies to my post than I expected. Thank you, everyone.<br /> <br /> Rose's mention of spotlight scenes helped me realize what my real difficulty is in running Vampire. One of the cardinal sins of GMing is, I've always understood, splitting the party. That combined with running exclusively online games (where it's even easier to lose players' attention and never even know it) makes me super reluctant to run &quot;spotlight scenes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given that Vampire is designed around allowing for them (which, it seems, is the source of most/all of my concerns with the system), maybe I just need to buckle down and risk trying it out.<br /> <br /> Thanks again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the issue with losing people's attention in online games. I've gotten away with it, but I see how that could be a problem. It's probably worth asking the players what they think, or how long they're willing to sit on the sidelines.<br /> <br /> One thing I do when running scenes without all of the players in them is let players run NPCs. That may not work for you, but I find it fun. It also lets me get more than one NPC active in a scene, something I struggle with doing on my own. (I can keep a lot of plates spinning in my brain, but two -- or more! -- separate personalities are very hard for me in realtime.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590792#post590792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys run scenes with different characters concurrently, or do one at a time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually one at a time. I <i>have</i> gotten fancy and cut back and forth between characters doing two different things, but it's really hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T07:53:34-07:00","id":591303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590794#post590794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Basically, split the party. Split it often and with impunity until the very concept of a 'party' (a tiresome D&amp;D holdover) is disillusioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Storyteller system I find it helps to not even think of the players' characters as &quot;a party&quot;. The players are &quot;the cast&quot; and their characters are the &quot;Dramatis person\u00e6&quot; for the story you're telling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T08:35:43-07:00","id":591368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=591007#post591007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Both. I've also run flashbacks...</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything he said here, second it. <br /> <br /> I like to fuck with framing and format as much as possible. <br /> <br /> My current favorite trick is calling &quot;CUT&quot; at a high point in a scene, and moving on from there. So we don't have the piddly shit that happens in wind down. <br /> <br /> But when I have a split thing going on, I usually pass rapidly around the table, one beat of action at a time as we resolve things. It creates tension, and gives everyone a moment or two to think about their next move, while enjoying what's going on in the other scenes. It feels a lot like a Guy Ritchie movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T11:11:22-07:00","id":591547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=591368#post591368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current favorite trick is calling &amp;quot;CUT&amp;quot; at a high point in a scene, and moving on from there. So we don't have the piddly shit that happens in wind down. <br /> <br /> But when I have a split thing going on, I usually pass rapidly around the table, one beat of action at a time as we resolve things. It creates tension, and gives everyone a moment or two to think about their next move, while enjoying what's going on in the other scenes. It feels a lot like a Guy Ritchie movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>One cannot stress enough how important cutting scenes is to roleplaying. Just imagine your favorite movie, now imagine if all the scenes dragged on until every character had their say and left the scene. <br /> <br /> Failing to end scenes is the number two death of games, right after everyone's schedules being too full. A scene that drags on loses all tension, all sense of urgency and purpose, and more often than not leaves the players confused with too much information. <br /> <br /> On that last note, I also recommend 'poking stick' characters. NPCs you can use to organically push scenes forward and cut the circle think that can occur when players start brainstorming. They also serve the purpose of letting the storyteller convey what he's hearing, thus curtailing miscommunication and disappointment in later scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:13:07-07:00","id":591653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=590792#post590792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys run scenes with different characters concurrently, or do one at a time?</div> </div> </div> </div> I run them at almost the same time, usually my players split themselves up (because they are assholes and they hate me) so generally i will start with one group and get them to the point where they are having an in character discussion, fight, scene, or something. then i will move to the next group while those players do that (my players know this enough to start getting to in character discussions with one another moderately easily, and then jump back and forth as I think of what happens next in the other world. <br /> <br /> Note: I do not advocate this method, it is haphazard and difficult it just works for me, at least when the party splits itself rather than having me do it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T16:08:49-07:00","id":591977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tunglashr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589689#post589689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So two evenly matched opponents should have a 10% chance to hit each other unless they spend willpower? That is as intended?<br /> <br /> The ridiculous example is exactly that, and noted. But two normal, reasonable characters have chance dice against each other. There are exactly three words that describe this: bad game design.<br /> <br /> If this were a non-combat situation involving a non-combat skill, and you had a character who had 2 dots in that skill, and was attempting an average difficultly action, you should expect to have around an 80% chance to succeed, no willpower necessary. But somehow, everyone in the world has forgotten how to do anything related to hand to hand combat. Either you are forced to spend a limited resource or forgo your defense to get a reasonable hit chance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure it does, hand to hand combat as evidenced above.<br /> <br /> If the normal situation in a game is completely broken because of all the possible crazy things the system tries to account for, then the veracity of those crazy things need to be seriously questioned. Evenly matched characters should not be relegated to a chance die. Arguing otherwise is like screaming at 2+2. No matter how loud you are, its still 4.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why so shortsighted?<br /> <br /> You say evenly matched people should have an 80% chance to succeed in imposing their skill over their opponent. <br /> <br /> So you have an 80% chance to hit an opponent, and that opponent has an 80 to avoid/block that hit.<br /> <br /> So whats the real chance of a event that has a 80% probability to happen that is followed by a 80% to cancel it?<br /> <br /> Someone better at math could answer that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T16:58:25-07:00","id":592064,"title":"","content":"16%. So a chance die is a little under but not by much. And the closer of the two options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T17:32:52-07:00","id":592121,"title":"","content":"Just to be fair to the Grognards who stick by the conventional wisdom about splitting the party, it's important to remember that D&amp;D emerged from miniature-based wargames, and started out as essentially a game about small unit combat tactics. Going into a dungeon basically meant that you were entering a warzone, so it was only natural that you'd always want somebody around to watch your six. Mind you, we're talking squad-sized units here; 8-14 guys wouldn't be all that unusual when you included henchmen and hirelings, and it was all but expected that some of them weren't going to make it out alive (in retrospect, that's probably why all the corridors were 10 feet wide, as well :P).<br /> <br /> Story, such as it existed, was there to provide some kind of justification for why the dungeon was there (more often than not, &quot;a wizard did it&quot;) and why anybody would go there (the answer always being some variation on the theme of buried treasure), and possibly to drop hints about what kinds of hazards might be inside (&quot;the Lair of the Werewolf King, you say? We should probably bring silver...&quot;). More complex plots could certainly develop over time, but they were more or less an optional feature.<br /> <br /> It's a perfectly enjoyable sort of game to play, but bears almost no resemblance to Vampire: the Requiem. As such, the same kind of advice doesn't really apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-15-2015, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T09:30:30-07:00","id":592760,"title":"","content":"Are you seriously going to bring D&amp;D to a V:tR forum just to show of prejudice?<br /> <br /> Lets just stick to the matter, WoD 2nd edition combat rules (because the rules in question aren't precisely from B&amp;S). They work, even if they seem a little strange to begin with. A single success can end a fight, and isn't that hard to achieve. The White Room combatants presented aren't equals, it is a comparison between a specialized hitter and a specialized defender. Willpower isn't a resource to be ignored, it is easy enough to recover and a fight is serious enough to spend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T18:37:10-07:00","id":597605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=592760#post592760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower isn't a resource to be ignored, it is easy enough to recover and a fight is serious enough to spend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely dependent on your Storyteller. It was always quite hard to recover in games I've been in.<br /> <br /> Everything aside, I do think chance to hit an opponent of comparable skill is too low in the system. I don't think &quot;use willpower&quot; is a good fix for it. More like a band aid. Such a resource should not be the default assumption just to make your combat system make sense, it is an extra to be pulled out when needed, sparingly. Is the combat unplayable? No, you can overcome this problem with resourcefulness. Does that mean there isn't a problem? I'm not sure I would call it a problem <i>exactly</i>, but it sure is less than ideal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T18:52:19-07:00","id":597643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=597605#post597605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entirely dependent on your Storyteller. It was always quite hard to recover in games I've been in.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is directly against the intent of the system. Take a look at the &quot;Rate of Return&quot; sidebar in the God Machine Chronicle (page 153.) According to the sidebar, player characters are supposed to be regaining a point of Willpower every few scenes on average, and Storytellers are supposed to give players who overspend Willpowerna few easy opportunities to indulge in their characters' Vices so they don't run out too quickly. Willpower is <i>supposed</i> to be easy to recover. The system, including combat, is designed with that expectation. You are free to go against that expectation, but unexpected issues may arise as a result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=597605#post597605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything aside, I do think chance to hit an opponent of comparable skill is too low in the system. I don't think &quot;use willpower&quot; is a good fix for it. More like a band aid. Such a resource should not be the default assumption just to make your combat system make sense, it is an extra to be pulled out when needed, sparingly. Is the combat unplayable? No, you can overcome this problem with resourcefulness. Does that mean there isn't a problem? I'm not sure I would call it a problem <i>exactly</i>, but it sure is less than ideal.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Use Willpower&quot; isn't supposed to be a fix, it's supposed to be what characters do when they want to make sure a roll succeeds. Generally a good policy in combat. Again, that's the system working as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-20-2015, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T19:00:05-07:00","id":597648,"title":"","content":"Also it's not so much about them being comparative skill. It's about one having enough skill and ability to avoid the combat skills and ability of another. Defense is there to defend, it's doing its job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T00:23:03-07:00","id":598017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=597643#post597643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is directly against the intent of the system. Take a look at the &quot;Rate of Return&quot; sidebar in the God Machine Chronicle (page 153.) According to the sidebar, player characters are supposed to be regaining a point of Willpower every few scenes on average, and Storytellers are supposed to give players who overspend Willpower a few easy opportunities to indulge in their characters' Vices so they don't run out too quickly. Willpower is <i>supposed</i> to be easy to recover. The system, including combat, is designed with that expectation. You are free to go against that expectation, but unexpected issues may arise as a result.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an ST, that can often be quite hard to manage. It's very easy for it to fall by the wayside while other more pressing or plot relevant things are happening so players burn through willpower and don't recover it easily. I don't think it's so much &quot;doing it wrong&quot; as &quot;doing it right can be difficult and can often work against the rest of the game&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with high defence as is, but from an attacker's perspective it can feel exceptionally difficult to get an edge around it. Considering your best option (if you don't have a means of ignoring defence, like firearms or inflicting a tilt) is to do an all-out attack (+2) with willpower (+3) on a pool that can very easily be a chance die to begin with and leaves you very vulnerable afterwards (because you sacrifice all your own defence). It can make it feel swingy and unreliable which has the potential to be frustrating, especially if you have characters who want to be reliable close-range combatants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T00:49:38-07:00","id":598039,"title":"","content":"My sugestion to everyone who have difficulty with WP reward: just give 1 each scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T04:37:11-07:00","id":598153,"title":"","content":"I agree that WP gain should be more frequent. That ST in particular is always very stingy when it comes to these resources in any system. There is no point pointing out how it is intended as he will just say he thinks that is boring and that he believes the game is better when WP needs to be rationed a bit. I've just learned to live with it when it is his turn to ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=597643#post597643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Use Willpower&quot; isn't supposed to be a fix, it's supposed to be what characters do when they want to make sure a roll succeeds. Generally a good policy in combat. Again, that's the system working as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using willpower when you want to succeed is good. Needing to use willpower to have more than an abysmally low chance at hitting someone with equal skill is bad. Especially for NPCs, because giving them a lot of willpower to spend usually feels unfair to the players, who have a greater need of conserving it. There are ways around it for vampires, but a system needs to be built on a solid foundation. And this is obviously a little clink in the system that does not quite work as intended. Really, nobody is saying the system is bad. People keep dragging everything and the kitchen sink into it, but in the end the situation, reduced only to its core principles, clearly has issues.<br /> <br /> Is this a game breaking problem? Again, no, since you almost never reduce a situation to the bare essentials in actual play. But the fact that the problem exists at any level of abstraction points to a weakness in the system and suggests it could have been done better. That is all.<br /> <br /> As an aside, all out attack is nice, but who wants to get a +2 against their opponent and then receive a +2 attack against 0 defense back? The first all out attack is not likely to do severe damage to the enemy but his return attack does (and he does not even need to all out), so it becomes a game of chicken, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T07:11:21-07:00","id":598317,"title":"","content":"There are other methods. Sneak attacks, ganging up on them, weapons, armour, clever tactics...<br /> <br /> +2 dice unarmed isn't much. +2 dice when you're holding a weapon may just tip the scales.<br /> <br /> All in all I think the system is working <i>exactly</i> as intended. You want to fight a guy as good at not being hit as you are at hitting? Going up and trying to slug them is not going to be the most effective way of doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:44:42-07:00","id":598450,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think it's a chink in the system. It is, in fact, working exactly as intended. You may not <i>like</i> the way it's intended to work, and that's fine, but it's unfair to say it's a weakness in the system. There are a lot of ways to get around high defense built into the system (one of which is &quot;own a gun&quot;), and the design intent is that you have to use those tools if you want to hit reliably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T10:13:54-07:00","id":598479,"title":"","content":"Oh, and as for the whole &quot;storyteller characters can spend willpower with impunity&quot; thing?<br /> <br /> Storytellers: Have your characters spend willpower like they actually need to work to get it back, ok? It's more realistic that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T10:59:21-07:00","id":598541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=598479#post598479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and as for the whole &quot;storyteller characters can spend willpower with impunity&quot; thing?<br /> <br /> Storytellers: Have your characters spend willpower like they actually need to work to get it back, ok? It's more realistic that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn I read a sidebar somewhere that recommended having NPCs start off with half their maximum Willpower in and given scene, but I can't seem to find it any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T11:07:32-07:00","id":598550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=598541#post598541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could have sworn I read a sidebar somewhere that recommended having NPCs start off with half their maximum Willpower in and given scene, but I can't seem to find it any more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 196 of GMC. I posted it in another thread a little bit ago.<br /> <br /> It basically comes down to NPCs that are around often enough can utilize Willpower like PCs. Major named NPCs can do half their max per scene. Mooks get one willpower per scene.<br /> <br /> I think there was one more &quot;level&quot; to it, but I can't recall off the top of my head.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T11:38:28-07:00","id":598575,"title":"","content":"I also remember this, somewhere in GMC. So yeah, an NPC should have AT MOST half his WP available at any given scene.<br /> <br /> But yeah, just to say again what other already said, it isn't about equal levels of hability. It is about offense vs defense.<br /> <br /> You want 6 of base attack pool? Strength 3, Brawl 3. That's pretty much a professional brawler, what means this guy also probably have some fighting styles merits. But lets ignore them for now.<br /> <br /> A defender with 6 of Defense will have Wits 3 PLUS Dexterity 3, what's much more hard to come by than 3 at just one stat. And it is even less likely that he will have also Strength 3 to hit as hard. Athletics 3 is maybe as likely as Brawl 3, but what it says about the guy? How much people out there really have Athletics as much as Brawl at 3?<br /> <br /> The probability of a high defense enemy is low, and of a balanced enemy is even lower. Only some specific athletes could reasonably be as trained in one as in the other, and athletes, themost likely to have high Defense, are also unlikely to want a fight in the first place. You'll have, even as a player, a WAY easier time being a hard hitter than a defensive guy. Specialy when you remember that high Defense means not agains firearms and weakens against numerous opponents.<br /> <br /> Remember them that you ARE talking about a White Room scenario, and I'm not talking about using your surroundings or using WP. I'm talking about weapons and buddies. Defense &amp; Attack are almost equals when you talk about two guys, one-on-one, using their hands. That's a bar fight, or a martial arts competition. A situation where people does very little real harm to each other. If you want to HURT someone, even IRL, you'll want an edge. Maybe a literal edge.<br /> <br /> Just using a melee weapon you already have a considerable advantage. Did you saw the rule for Beaten Down? If you don't use it, so your fights aren't that reallistical to begin with, because when someone wants to live, and most people do, they do leave a fight as early as they start to get hurt. With a weapon you add direct damage, plus your successes, and it is Lethal damage. Well, to a mortal you give the Beaten Down Tilt with ANY Lethal, so we already have an edge here. Even if it wasn't so simple, the tilt would trigger with damage equal to Stamina, and most people have 2 Stamina. Or do you REALLY think that common someone with Dexterity 3, Wits 3, Stamina 3 and Athletics 3? Don't forget other tilts and the fact that isn't so hard to find a heavier weapon.<br /> <br /> Ganging up on someone is another way, since you reduce the target's Defense at each turn. So you can pretty much turn anyone into a bloody pulp just ganging up on him with your buddies. If you are alone and without a weapon, you shouldn't enter a serious fight to begin with. And the WP comes in handy precisely because you are fighting for your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T11:46:23-07:00","id":598584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=598153#post598153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using willpower when you want to succeed is good. Needing to use willpower to have more than an abysmally low chance at hitting someone with equal skill is bad. Especially for NPCs, because giving them a lot of willpower to spend usually feels unfair to the players, who have a greater need of conserving it. There are ways around it for vampires, but a system needs to be built on a solid foundation. And this is obviously a little clink in the system that does not quite work as intended. Really, nobody is saying the system is bad. People keep dragging everything and the kitchen sink into it, but in the end the situation, reduced only to its core principles, clearly has issues.<br /> <br /> Is this a game breaking problem? Again, no, since you almost never reduce a situation to the bare essentials in actual play. But the fact that the problem exists at any level of abstraction points to a weakness in the system and suggests it could have been done better. That is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'm inclined to disagree. In a struggle between equals I want it to be the decisions, not the dice that decide the outcome. If, in this mirror fighter scenario we have going, either party leaves the fight as anything but exhausted mentally and physically then I'd be hard pressed to call it a fight between equals.<br /> <br /> Lets remove dice from the scenario and just look at it naratively (as this is the Storytelling system, and therefore it should strive simulate <b>stories</b>). When two characters of 'equivalent' skill go head to head in most media the fight is generally long and drawn out, occurring at a climactic moment, with minutes spent as the characters trade blows and vie for position. In the end even the victorious party is quite spent. I think I can safely say that the victorious character could be rightly declared low on Health and Willpower, having exhausted both during the fight (indeed, it is common in stories for this to be the moment where a much weaker character, who would not normally have stood a chance, can step in an seize victory over his less-than-prime combatant).<br /> <br /> Stepping back to the system, I'm of the opinion that a fight between equals should be a bit of a slog. With the caveat that the storyteller should be careful to restrict such encounters to climactic moments where the low dice pools and diminishing resources generate tension, not boredom. As a practical example: <i>I ran a game, the setting of which is largely irrelevant, wherein two players happened to be playing swordsmen of different veins (one a very quick duelist and the other heavily armed and armored). More importantly both were on opposite sides of the conflict and, as the story progressed, the other players began to expect and look forward to the encounter. Thus, when the two met in single combat at the climax of the final session, the untouchable defense of one and impenetrable armor of the other did not render the fight boring. Quite the contrary, each character was stretched to the limits of their options and forced to fight with considerably more care and cunning than they had up till that point.</i><br /> <br /> TL;DR - It's not that fights between equals are broken. They have a place, and it's the storyteller's job to build enough tension that low dice pools and dwindling resources is climactic, not boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 07-21-2015, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T20:41:30-07:00","id":598972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=598550#post598550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Page 196 of GMC. I posted it in another thread a little bit ago.<br /> <br /> It basically comes down to NPCs that are around often enough can utilize Willpower like PCs. Major named NPCs can do half their max per scene. Mooks get one willpower per scene.<br /> <br /> I think there was one more &quot;level&quot; to it, but I can't recall off the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks. Yeah, the one Willpower was actually for minor named NPCs and mooks get no Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T00:07:17-07:00","id":605347,"title":"","content":"Please note that professional fighters at the top of their game take <i>dozens</i> of significant hits in a fight, many walk away still standing (so didn't fill their Bashing track) and have accuracy rates in the 40-50% range.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.fightmetric.com/event-details/0c3838c8f7c620c2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fightmetric.com/event-details/0c3838c8f7c620c2\" target=\"_blank\"> Loading&hellip; </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fightmetric.com/event-details/0c3838c8f7c620c2\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.fightmetric.com/event-details/0c3838c8f7c620c2 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In this fight, which was Fight of the Night and involved no grappling of note, so is as close as I can see the 'just rolling brawl at each other' as we're going to get between two well matched opponents (a fight in which one side utterly dominates rarely wins fight of the night)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.fightmetric.com/fight-details/c97e99ca5422f03b\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fightmetric.com/fight-details/c97e99ca5422f03b\" target=\"_blank\"> Loading&hellip; </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fightmetric.com/fight-details/c97e99ca5422f03b\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.fightmetric.com/fight-details/c97e99ca5422f03b </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edson throws 135 <i>significant</i> strikes, landing 64 of them for 47% accuracy while his opponent Paul throws 150 significant strikes, only landing 47 for 31% accuracy. Seems to me that Paul is rolling 1 die (not a chance die) on his attacks while Edson is rolling somewhere between 1 and 2 dice, we'll give him 2 dice.<br /> <br /> Now, yes, these are professional fighters at the top of their game so, no, they don't represent the 'wo/man in the street' having a fight all that well, but it's something interesting at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#232B31\"><span style=\"font-family:Robotoregular\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A quick definition: significant strikes refer to all strikes at distance and power strikes in the clinch and on the ground. It does not include small, short strikes in the clinch and on the ground. Those will be included in the Total Strikes category.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T00:48:39-07:00","id":605374,"title":"","content":"If we were to model the aforementioned Paul-Edson fight in vampire, we obviously couldn't count all of the significant strikes that connected as successful attacks, since successful attacks always do at least a point of damage and nobody has 64+ health boxes. We might say that a single successful attack represents more than one significant strike and/or decide that some (presumably arbitrary) number of blows which connect will nevertheless be counted as failed attacks. The former method seems preferable; if we use the latter, we could fudge the accuracy to be within whatever range we want (as long as it's lower than the actual observed accuracy) by turning hits into misses. That said, it's possible that it would be accurate to say that some strikes that meet the criteria to be considered &quot;significant&quot; do not, in fact, significantly contribute to the damage inflicted on the opposing fighter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T01:31:39-07:00","id":605406,"title":"","content":"As CatDoom said, one roll does not equate to one punch (or shot, or sword swing, etc). nWoD's combat system is a narrative abstraction, even the idea that one round is equal to three seconds is merely a ballpark suggestion. One can easily run turns as ten to fifteen seconds (or more) of trading blows, or drop rounds down to fractions of seconds as two high-powered combatants go head to head at impossible speed. All things bend to the story's needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T02:27:45-07:00","id":605423,"title":"","content":"In fact, I never saw a system where every hit on dice meant a hit on fiction AND the result was even near of being realistic. Not even D&amp;D tries to assume that 1 dice roll equals just 1 strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T03:24:57-07:00","id":605435,"title":"","content":"Arguably GURPS with its 1 second combat rounds?<br /> <br /> But yes, one point I was making with my post was that there is no way nWoD combat is trying to make it so every hit or attack is a roll. In fact nWoD combat is probably more accurately representing the 'highlight reel' exchanges in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T10:33:33-07:00","id":605685,"title":"","content":"Most systems are already unrealistic in that they try so hard they end up with unbelievable short fights time-wise (surely not so much from game perspetive, where each turn do take some time to resolve). So... no, not even GURPS. IRL fights rarely resolve in so few seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T04:49:24-07:00","id":606477,"title":"","content":"In my experience, a real life street fight doesn't last upwards of thirty seconds, if that. But that's still ten turns, which a long time for combat. And if one of the combatants outmatches another by enough, that time is <i>drastically</i> reduced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T07:24:02-07:00","id":606543,"title":"","content":"In my experience, in most RPGs the equivalent of a street fight will last 1 to 3 turns. Anything more for such a simple fight will be simply boring. And that means 9 seconds in WoD, 18 seconds in D&amp;D and 3 seconds in GURPS, at most. The kind of combat that usualy takes some minutes IRL and several minutes in movies, in RPGs usualy takes from 6 to 15 turns, rarely more than that, and again you have at most 45 seconds in WoD, 1 and a half minute in D&amp;D and 15 seconds in GURPS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T14:56:51-07:00","id":607160,"title":"","content":"I think how quickly they end is sort of nice when the thing they're going for is that sort of shocking violence simulator.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of that scene in <i>Inglorious Basterds</i>, in the pub when the shootout happens. It's very sudden, very violent, and a bunch of people are dead at the end, and that's struck me as appropriate for the level of sudden violence you might see in a mortals on mortals fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:54:35-07:00","id":607284,"title":"","content":"As someone said above... dice rolls are an abstraction and time can practically be whatever fits the narrative. Turns don't even need to have the same length of time in the same fighting scene.Whatever fits the narrative and the intent of the characters in it determines how long a violent scene last.<br /> <br /> If a person is assaulted in an apartment by two thugs while a friend witness it from the streets through the window it can look like this...<br /> <br /> Turn 1... the intent of the assaulted person in the apartment is to avoid harm until help arrives. The friend on the street start running up the stairs to the apartment. The friend roll a Dex+Athletics roll for running up the stairs. The GM decide to give a bonus or penalty to the assaulted persons dodge roll, depending on the friends roll and the first part of the combat are pretty much done as one turn. Any damage dealt become part of the narrative and become the condition of the fight as the friend arrive.<br /> Turn 2+ After this point new intents are declared and several turns which have a shorter interval in terms of time are concluded.<br /> <br /> This would fit well with the narrative and keep the game pace flowing fast and the drama flowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7068,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","user":"JorgenCAB","date":". 07-30-2015, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T18:29:05-07:00","id":624863,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, something occurred to me about the example of the fighters trading blows: I bet money you'd model the ability to take a lot more hits with the narrative abstraction of hits that miss (mechanically, maybe they connected but the damage or pain was negligible) <i>or </i>they might have traits like Iron Skin and are able to shrug off a lot of successful hits through that. Just a fun little thought about tough guys like this fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T02:14:00-07:00","id":625224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tunglashr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589629-blood-and-smoke-combat-question?p=589689#post589689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So two evenly matched opponents should have a 10% chance to hit each other unless they spend willpower? That is as intended?<br /> <br /> The ridiculous example is exactly that, and noted. But two normal, reasonable characters have chance dice against each other. There are exactly three words that describe this: bad game design.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I practice martials art and fighting sport since I was 15 years old. But even without these kind experience if you see a normal box match on tv you could argue it. Hit with a single full strenght punch or kick is extremely difficult. Usually in a real combat the two fighter use fake hits and multiple (not full strenght) attack just to breack the guard of the opponent and at the right moment try to hit with the strong one. in this sense, this combat sistem work pretty good and in a realistic way. I know that for a game it could be frustrating...anyway as other told above, there are a lot of way to surclass defense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}